          "title": "You'll want to know: le braquage",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le braquage — \"the armed robbery, the hold-up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le braquage de la banque a duré dix minutes. The bank robbery lasted ten minutes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informal but frequent in the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "braquage is built with -age on the verb meaning \"to aim, to point (a gun)\"; the origin of that verb is not settled (EtymDB lists no parent)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
