              "text": "échapper — \"to escape; to slip from (one's hands)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un des braqueurs s'est échappé par le toit. One of the robbers escaped over the roof."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Used both ways. With se for breaking out: s'échapper de prison. Without se, with à: échapper à un danger — to escape a danger."
            }
          ]
        },
